### Contrat API flows ETL (D18) — exemples de requêtes/réponses.
### Source de vérité = Postgres (flow_versions append-only) ; flows.json
### n'est qu'un artefact projeté au deploy. Cf. docs/architecture/flow-engine.md.
###
### Erreurs : 400 champ-par-champ forme DRF {"<champ>": msg} ou
### {"violations": [...]} pour un graphe invalide ; 409 {"error": "conflict",
### "description": ...} si expected_version_number périmé (concurrence
### optimiste — écart assumé vs 400) ; 503 {"error": "flow_runtime"} si le
### moteur est coupé (settings.flow.enabled=false) ou sans acquittement.

### Créer un flow (flow + version 1 en une transaction) — 201
POST http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "pipeline température",
  "device_id": null,
  "author": "alice",
  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "n1", "kind": "inject",
        "config": { "repeat_secs": 60.0, "payload": null },
        "outputs": [{ "port": 0, "targets": ["n2"] }]
      },
      {
        "id": "n2", "kind": "pnex_sql",
        "config": { "query": "SELECT 1", "params": [] },
        "outputs": [{ "port": 0, "targets": ["n3"] }]
      },
      { "id": "n3", "kind": "debug", "config": {} }
    ]
  }
}

### 201 →
### {
###   "id": 1, "org_id": 1, "device_id": null,
###   "name": "pipeline température", "status": "draft",
###   "deployed_version_number": null, "latest_version_number": 1,
###   "graph": { ... }, "created_at": "...", "updated_at": "..."
### }

### Lister les flows de l'org (D14 : {count, next, previous, results})
### Filtres : search (nom), status (draft|deployed|error)
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows?search=température&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Détail d'un flow (graphe de la dernière version)
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Enregistrer une NOUVELLE version (append-only ; aucun rechargement
### runtime — le déploiement est une action séparée).
### 409 si expected_version_number ≠ version courante.
PATCH http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expected_version_number": 1,
  "note": "double la fréquence",
  "author": "alice",
  "graph": { "nodes": [] }
}

### Historique (paginé, ordre descendant) ; "deployed": true sur la version
### actuellement publiée.
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Graphe d'une version précise (audit/rollback)
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1/versions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### Déployer une version (absent = dernière) → reprojection de TOUS les flows
### déployés de l'instance + rechargement à chaud (SIGUSR1). 503 si le moteur
### est coupé. Rollback = même appel sur une version antérieure.
POST http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1/deploy
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version_number": 2 }

### Rollback explicite (alias sémantique du deploy)
POST http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1/rollback
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version_number": 1 }

### État du runtime vu par le superviseur
GET http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1/runtime
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}

### 200 →
### { "running": true, "pid": 4242, "restarts": 1,
###   "deployed_flow_id": 1, "deployed_version_number": 2 }

### Supprimer (204 ; versions en cascade ; artefact reprojeté si déployé)
DELETE http://localhost:5150/api/v1/flows/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-Id: {{org_id}}
